 <div class="method"><strong>Intent decisions and crop pixels are different measurements.</strong>
 <p>Passive intent targets, explicit interactions, GT-geometry policy targets, no-target negatives and rule fixtures are separate cohorts. There is no combined accuracy headline. The scene-v1 ranker and semantic-v2 consume the same frozen seven-noun detections; production scene-v1 uses five nouns and has not been remeasured here. Controlled mode supplies GT-derived detector fixtures and named faults. It is a rule/crop regression, not detector accuracy.</p>
 <p>Decision metrics compare the chosen region's assigned target ID. Pixel metrics compare the actual emitted crop with the original photo inside the keep mask, independently of that ID. Identical full-frame outputs therefore receive identical label retention and target coverage. Full-frame context can preserve every label pixel and retain every distractor: read both columns. No wine identity accuracy is measured. COCO uses a generic bottle category; the beverage identity of every imported bottle has not been independently verified.</p>
